ttps://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T05:31:22-07:00","id":1399268,"title":"","content":"But a Tremere essay would be as bad as your sabbat essay. A less controversial topic would be... So I guess people don't actually care much about the Hecata? Like,I don't like at all what they've done there but I've never really cared all that much about necromancers anyway and I think most are in the same boat there. <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd like to see someone talk about how the disciplines have changed and how to adapt to them. Sure we'd get into arguments and stuff but it'd be a good productive discussion to talk about how the masquerade works now that many key disciplines got nerfed. <br /> <br /> You could also talk about how resonances work and how we're supposed to find people that give us XP for disciplines and hoard them like they're gold because xp is difficult now and we want to abuse the system as much as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T05:38:18-07:00","id":1399269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399268#post1399268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a Tremere essay would be as bad as your sabbat essay. A less controversial topic would be... So I guess people don't actually care much about the Hecata? Like,I don't like at all what they've done there but I've never really cared all that much about necromancers anyway and I think most are in the same boat there.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd like to see someone talk about how the disciplines have changed and how to adapt to them. Sure we'd get into arguments and stuff but it'd be a good productive discussion to talk about how the masquerade works now that many key disciplines got nerfed.<br /> <br /> You could also talk about how resonances work and how we're supposed to find people that give us XP for disciplines and hoard them like they're gold because xp is difficult now and we want to abuse the system as much as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good suggestions. Mostly my interest is in setting elements as I'm a very light on rules kind of guy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T11:47:18-07:00","id":1399342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399269#post1399269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very good suggestions. Mostly my interest is in setting elements as I'm a very light on rules kind of guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>do a tremere one, I wanna see it<br /> <br /> I've noticed a considerable decline of threads on them lately<br /> <br /> a few years back, 9 threads out of 10 were about tremere and thaumaturgy<br /> (not that I'm complaining, just funny how the tables have turned)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T12:33:49-07:00","id":1399351,"title":"","content":"There's a lot less appeal to playing them now though. They don't have thaumaturgy. Their other disciplines were hit pretty hard, Their weakness is silly. It's all just flavour. Which you may or may not like. For V5 tremere get to say &quot;I'm a witch&quot; but that really just means they have a discipline with a few rituals. The clan's throat is beneath a writer's pen and it looks like they're on their way out. They're salvagable, but who wants to invest in a company that's getting less valuable? <br /> <br /> I've grown to like the false-carna split, but that's not confirmed canon (and probably isn't despite logic), and pretty much all else looks bad for the clan. <br /> <br /> Who rolls up to a V5 game and picks Tremere? Advanced players don't get the spells and basic players have a lot of baggage without much incentive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-0