SIS. The IS where no big deal then. Al'quaida would have been way more believable and I still hope, that they will retcon that like that vampires made a gay massacer just for having experimental material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T11:29:38-07:00","id":1399888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399886#post1399886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well there they protested, that it is to visitable and clearly is to high tech for terrorists. So it would have been much better if they would have went with either LKW or airplanes loaded with dynamite and blowed them up there. My other problem is, that they said it whas ISIS. The IS where no big deal then. Al'quaida would have been way more believable and I still hope, that they will retcon that like that vampires made a gay massacer just for having experimental material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it depends, &quot;who is reporting and investigating what happened there?&quot;<br /> <br /> And gay massacre?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T11:54:37-07:00","id":1399891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399888#post1399888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And gay massacre?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Chechnya is actually vampires!&quot; debacle from the first printings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T12:08:14-07:00","id":1399893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399812#post1399812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, V5 has really developed thin-bloods in a much more original way and even culturally than previous editions; I love the whole aspect of thin-blood alchemy; makes it possible for players to home-brew known discipline powers. Really liking how they are being treated in this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can totally relate to that. Seeing one of my players playing a thin blood, was one of the things in V5 turning me from wanting to play a one shot for old times sake to buying all V5-stuff there is and planning a whole chronicle (which is still running).<br /> <br /> I thought saying out loud that one like Blood Alchemy was kind of a 'don't' in the internet. At least I got that impression on reddit. But yeah, I really like the post-modern touch to Blood Alchemy. Reminds me a bit of 'Unknown Armies - Lite'. If I want hermetic magic true to historical hermeticism I play Ars Magica, because WoD never did hermeticism too well. So I really liked the change in style. Just some very unclearly phrased rulings were a problem. It seems like virtually every player/ST I asked about Alchemy rules interpreted them in a different way. There should be some rephrasings and some more actual play examples for the next printing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T12:32:51-07:00","id":1399895,"title":"","content":"Magic is not meant to be post modern. It works because people believe in rules; an absence of rules mean it cannot work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T12:40:18-07:00","id":1399897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399895#post1399895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic is not meant to be post modern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Traditions have left the chat","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T12:48:32-07:00","id":1399898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399895#post1399895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic is not meant to be post modern. It works because people believe in rules; an absence of rules mean it cannot work.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Can't work&quot; as in wouldn't make sense from a narrative point of view? Or &quot;can't work&quot; as in &quot;does actually not work&quot;? If you mean the first one: Ok cool, tell that to Unknown Armies, because it works well there. If you mean the second one: Oookay. *Homer Simpson fading backwards through the hedge-gif*<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T13:47:35-07:00","id":1399906,"title":"","content":"Quite obviously, i meant the second. Post modernism is not a paradigm to get results. Magic requires strong, connected beliefs, where symbols carry important meaning and must be used in conjunction with one another, Post modernism is a system where you can pick and choose beliefs at the drop of a hat and don't need to interconnect them. Therefore, you can't be an actual postmodern mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even Chaos sorcery and punk magic relies on the framework of a belief system, it isn't just do whatever you like, it's do some unorthadox yet symbolic actions; you get high, listen to <i>Veteran of the psychic wars</i>, and graffiti someone's house to give them the feelings you felt in the song. You don't put abraxo into a pool of blood and drink it to get super powers. What does Abraxo symbolise to you? Doing random shit for the postmodern lulz doesn't facilitate magic, you've got to actually structure the joke. You need people to say &quot;I get it, very clever&quot; rather than &quot;what?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T13:55:06-07:00","id":1399907,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26196_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26196\" data-vbnamecard=\"26196\">Saturno</a> never heard of Unknown Armies before, is it like a mage game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T14:34:07-07:00","id":1399910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399906#post1399906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite obviously, i meant the second. Post modernism is not a paradigm to get results. Magic requires strong, connected beliefs, where symbols carry important meaning and must be used in conjunction with one another, Post modernism is a system where you can pick and choose beliefs at the drop of a hat and don't need to interconnect them. Therefore, you can't be an actual postmodern mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I was half-joking, but as you say you actually believe in magic, I think we hit hard rock. (Or did I misunderstand you? Do you believe in magic working in reality or is it about verisimilitude as an aesthetic concept? because if it's the latter then we want the same thing.) Because I don't believe in magic and I only studied historical magical texts as part of my studies for history of philosophy and that's were my point of view comes from and that's what I use as an influence for RPG sessions. Your worldview seems to be radically different from mine (and that's of course not for me to judge) to the point that we are not really talking about magic as a sujet or narrative concept for a RPG anymore. And I find it hard to talk about magic as if it were a real thing that would be considered a valid influence in our century. So, no offense, but I don't think we will have much fun taking this further.<br /> <br /> Just this one thing: For narrative reasons I wouldn't push postmodern magic too far. So you're right. It shouldn't be random. That's what I pay attention to while STing a game.<br /> Oh, and please take my like for the Blue \u00d6yster Cult reference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399907#post1399907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26196_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26196\" data-vbnamecard=\"26196\">Saturno</a> never heard of Unknown Armies before, is it like a mage game?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a kind of Mage game if David Lynch directed it. Pretty nice, pretty whack and pretty much indepted to the postmodern paradigma. (But at the same time not random. I has the approach that MyWifeIsScary described for chaos magic. The 'very clever, I get it' one.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":26196,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","user":"Saturno","date":". 06-29-2020, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T14:44:52-07:00","id":1399912,"title":"","content":"So... you think I believe in magic in real life and that i think it's neccessary to believe in magic in real life to believe in magic in game?<br /> <br /> That's... a first. <br /> <br /> What i am saying is, your <i>character</i> needs absolutely concrete beliefs with good internal logic. <br /> <br /> It's helpful if you (the player) know what those are, but not entirely neccessary, so long as you don't insist in a 'lol random' paradigm-not-really-a-paradigm it's all fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T15:01:38-07:00","id":1399916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399912#post1399912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... you think I believe in magic in real life and that i think it's neccessary to believe in magic in real life to believe in magic in game?<br /> <br /> That's... a first.<br /> <br /> What i am saying is, your <i>character</i> needs absolutely concrete beliefs with good internal logic.<br /> <br /> It's helpful if you (the player) know what those are, but not entirely neccessary, so long as you don't insist in a 'lol random' paradigm-not-really-a-paradigm it's all fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry then, I didn't want to assume. That's really what I got from your answer (&quot;obviously it's the latter one&quot;).<br /> My apologies. That was not supposed to be polemic.<br /> <br /> If it's about verisimilitude, I'm all with you. Blood Alchemy should have something that makes sense and is not random. There should be an inner logic. But as the formulae in the core rule book are just examples for a formula, I never got the idea that V5's Blood Alchemy couldn't be interpreted in a more rational way.<br /> <br /> That's why I mentioned Unknown Armies, because it takes the moniker of postmodern magic, but at the same time limits the degree of randomness to a point were there's an internal logic of an individual's magic, (and that logic might only be sufficient for him) but him believing it with existential conviction makes it real and affecting the world. That's what I see as a possible interpretation/route for V5's Blood Alchemy too and that's what I like.<br /> <br /> Apologies again. I would let my last posting stand as it is if that's ok with you. If you find it offensive I could also edit it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T15:33:04-07:00","id":1399925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399912#post1399912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... you think I believe in magic in real life and that i think it's neccessary to believe in magic in real life to believe in magic in game?<br /> <br /> That's... a first.<br /> <br /> What i am saying is, your <i>character</i> needs absolutely concrete beliefs with good internal logic.<br /> <br /> It's helpful if you (the player) know what those are, but not entirely neccessary, so long as you don't insist in a 'lol random' paradigm-not-really-a-paradigm it's all fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying that Thin-Blood Alchemy should depend on the beliefs of the alchemist, like M:tA magic, rather than the physical process itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T16:19:08-07:00","id":1399934,"title":"","content":"It's magic, so yes. The beliefs and the physical process shoukd intertwine to make a workable paradigm. EG gold and mercury have their symbolism, milk has it's symbolism, avocadoes have symbolism. Mixing blood with something you find symbolic should yeild results related to that symbolism. (The gold improves the body, the mercury purifies it, the milk helps you look younger, the avocado helps you take photos... ) <br /> <br /> Alchemy historically.... it's a good read. I recomend you look it up. some surprising stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T16:42:12-07:00","id":1399940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399934#post1399934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's magic, so yes. The beliefs and the physical process shoukd intertwine to make a workable paradigm. EG gold and mercury have their symbolism, milk has it's symbolism, avocadoes have symbolism. Mixing blood with something you find symbolic should yeild results related to that symbolism. (The gold improves the body, the mercury purifies it, the milk helps you look younger, the avocado helps you take photos... )<br /> <br /> Alchemy historically.... it's a good read. I recomend you look it up. some surprising stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was real alchemy believed to function by beliefs in symbols? I thought the point of a lot of what alchemists did was to discover the mechanisms of natural physical and spiritual processes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T16:47:02-07:00","id":1399941,"title":"","content":"Well I don't think Thin Blood Alchemy is meant to be especially post-modern. It's just that Thin Blood blood is super-duper magical so they can harness it with Resonance blood and other Kindred blood plus other stuff.<br /> <br /> So, yes, drinking from a depressed guy and mixing it with Taco Bell=Lure of the Flames.<br /> <br /> I think it exists basically to justify the Resonance system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T16:49:36-07:00","id":1399942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399934#post1399934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's magic, so yes. The beliefs and the physical process shoukd intertwine to make a workable paradigm. EG gold and mercury have their symbolism, milk has it's symbolism, avocadoes have symbolism. <b>Mixing blood with something you find symbolic should yeild results related to that symbolism.</b> (The gold improves the body, the mercury purifies it, the milk helps you look younger, the avocado helps you take photos... )</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that's what TBA's paradigm is supposed to be, the book just doesn't explain it that directly.<br /> <br /> For example, look at what's required for the level-one formula <i>Haze</i>, which produces a cloud of mist or fog:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ingredients: In addition to the alchemist\u2019s Blood and phlegmatic human blood, dry ice or cigar smoke or auto exhaust </div> </div> </div>Nothing especially deep or obscure there, but it's easy to see how dry ice, cigar smoke, and auto exhaust would be symbolically linked to fog.<br /> <br /> For a higher-level ritual, see <i>Airborne Momentum</i>, which lets you fly briefly:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ingredients: The alchemist\u2019s Blood, choleric and sanguine human blood, champagne, bird blood, helium, scopolamine or belladonna extract </div> </div> </div>A little bit less\u2026on-the-nose\u2026than <i>Haze</i>, but all of those things are still symbolically linked to flight. I wouldn't be surprised to see a MtAs Mage using any of those in a flight spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T18:24:53-07:00","id":1399964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399886#post1399886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well there they protested, that it is to visitable and clearly is to high tech for terrorists. So it would have been much better if they would have went with either LKW or airplanes loaded with dynamite and blowed them up there. My other problem is, that they said it whas ISIS. The IS where no big deal then. Al'quaida would have been way more believable and I still hope, that they will retcon that like that vampires made a gay massacer just for having experimental material.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Logically, most people wouldn't have even seen the drones, there would just have been a boom and then military moving in, like happens, with a cordon later. That's... pretty much how that works. The cover of the bomb that terrorists were working on went off is easily acceptable by the largest amount of the populace. Occam's Razor and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T01:31:37-07:00","id":1400024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399940#post1399940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was real alchemy believed to function by beliefs in symbols? I thought the point of a lot of what alchemists did was to discover the mechanisms of natural physical and spiritual processes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Early alchemy was more based on their respective level of natural philosophy. That shifted at least gradually during the late antiquity (and especially in the hermetic schools), when a rise of less 'practical' and more introspective ways of alchemy was happening.<br /> <br /> But there is no hard distinction between alchemy based on natural philosophy and alchemy based on symbols and refinement of the alchemists soul. It's a gradual one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399941#post1399941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I don't think Thin Blood Alchemy is meant to be especially post-modern. It's just that Thin Blood blood is super-duper magical so they can harness it with Resonance blood and other Kindred blood plus other stuff.<br /> <br /> So, yes, drinking from a depressed guy and mixing it with Taco Bell=Lure of the Flames.<br /> <br /> I think it exists basically to justify the Resonance system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm ... But the resonance system isn't played too straight as well, is it? I mean on p.226 it's described as one of many kindred systems to categorize blood and there are many others who work just as well although they work pretty different. If several theories that contradict each other come to the same conclusion/work just as well that's at least a bit post-modern and not very plausible. But then the whole thing, that the four humours are a thing and are to found inside people reliably is already a bit of a stretch. (Although a nice one for narrative purpose. My players had never had so much fun hunting as in V5.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399942#post1399942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe that's what TBA's paradigm is supposed to be, the book just doesn't explain it that directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought too and how we use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T05:44:07-07:00","id":1400055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saturno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1400024#post1400024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Early alchemy was more based on their respective level of natural philosophy. That shifted at least gradually during the late antiquity (and especially in the hermetic schools), when a rise of less 'practical' and more introspective ways of alchemy was happening.<br /> <br /> But there is no hard distinction between alchemy based on natural philosophy and alchemy based on symbols and refinement of the alchemists soul. It's a gradual one.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I don't think that the symbolism matters in-universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T08:32:40-07:00","id":1400095,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399942#post1399942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe that's what TBA's paradigm is supposed to be, the book just doesn't explain it that directly.<br /> <br /> For example, look at what's required for the level-one formula <i>Haze</i>, which produces a cloud of mist or fog:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nothing especially deep or obscure there, but it's easy to see how dry ice, cigar smoke, and auto exhaust would be symbolically linked to fog.<br /> <br /> For a higher-level ritual, see <i>Airborne Momentum</i>, which lets you fly briefly:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A little bit less\u2026on-the-nose\u2026than <i>Haze</i>, but all of those things are still symbolically linked to flight. I wouldn't be surprised to see a MtAs Mage using any of those in a flight spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some fair points here. <br /> But the book also encourages you to be a fish-malk type alchemist and generates colourful descriptions of Thin blood alchemists trying out the kind of shit that'd have Tremere up at noon. I do recall one description of how a spell works as.. kinda like trying to hold up an elephant with a single layer of toilet paper. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1399941#post1399941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I don't think Thin Blood Alchemy is meant to be especially post-modern. It's just that Thin Blood blood is super-duper magical so they can harness it with Resonance blood and other Kindred blood plus other stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinblood blood is less magical. That's like, their whole deal. Are ghouls and revenants more magical than vampires now? </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, yes, drinking from a depressed guy and mixing it with Taco Bell=Lure of the Flames. </div> </div> </div> Fishmalk territory. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it exists basically to justify the Resonance system. </div> </div> </div>The Resonance system is something that, while it needs a lot of work, is actually a decent V5 thing. I think Thinblood alchemy actually delegitimises it by making it a thing for kooky thinbloods. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T08:34:37-07:00","id":1400096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thinblood blood is less magical. That's like, their whole deal. Are ghouls and revenants more magical than vampires now? </div> </div> </div>Uh, yes, have you read OUTCASTS?<br /> <br /> They explictly state that Caitiff and Thin Bloods have the ability to create their own Disciplines due to their fluidity of their blood.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T08:55:11-07:00","id":1400103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1400055#post1400055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why I don't think that the symbolism matters in-universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by that exactly?<br /> I don't think the symbolism <u>has</u> to matter, because there are other ways to make alchemy explainable or 'realistic', but as the historical diversity of alchemy demonstrates symbolism could be <u>a possible way</u> to explain it. Also the approach via natural philosophy and via symbolism are not mutually exclusive. They could well work like a scale. For example Jabir ibn Hayyan used hotness and moistness as means to categorize elements, but his explanations why he does so sometimes make use of symbols. Furthermore it's sometimes hard to decide wether an explanation with which we are confronted in alchemy is supposed to be symbolic or metaphoric. Additionaly, during the renaissance we are confronted with the problem that terms/phrases which sound like they could be symbolic or metaphoric might as well be cyphers for otherwise pretty mundane science stuff in order to make them obscure to other alchemists and to protect your own findings.<br /> <br /> So depending on the background of the alchemist there are many possibilities. My take would be to refrain from treating TBA like a modern science as a ST (because the core rule book doesn't support this too strongly) and to treat it more like philosophy or classical poetry (which means poetry that has rules but which doesn't work bijective). As a player or character you could of course treat your concrete version of TBA as a science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T11:21:54-07:00","id":1400142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1400095#post1400095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the book also encourages you to be a fish-malk type alchemist and generates colourful descriptions of Thin blood alchemists trying out the kind of shit that'd have Tremere up at noon. I do recall one description of how a spell works as.. kinda like trying to hold up an elephant with a single layer of toilet paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which parts in particular? If we're thinking of the same description, that's an outsider who doesn't understand what's going on being grossed out by the practices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1400095#post1400095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinblood blood is less magical. That's like, their whole deal. Are ghouls and revenants more magical than vampires now?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less <i>vampiric</i>, but has also always been able to do things fullbloods couldn't do. Alchemy is them discovering a paradigm to formalize their things fullbloods couldn't do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T12:13:41-07:00","id":1400153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saturno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1400103#post1400103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you mean by that exactly?<br /> I don't think the symbolism <u>has</u> to matter, because there are other ways to make alchemy explainable or 'realistic', but as the historical diversity of alchemy demonstrates symbolism could be <u>a possible way</u> to explain it. Also the approach via natural philosophy and via symbolism are not mutually exclusive. They could well work like a scale. For example Jabir ibn Hayyan used hotness and moistness as means to categorize elements, but his explanations why he does so sometimes make use of symbols. Furthermore it's sometimes hard to decide wether an explanation with which we are confronted in alchemy is supposed to be symbolic or metaphoric. Additionaly, during the renaissance we are confronted with the problem that terms/phrases which sound like they could be symbolic or metaphoric might as well be cyphers for otherwise pretty mundane science stuff in order to make them obscure to other alchemists and to protect your own findings.<br /> <br /> So depending on the background of the alchemist there are many possibilities. My take would be to refrain from treating TBA like a modern science as a ST (because the core rule book doesn't support this too strongly) and to treat it more like philosophy or classical poetry (which means poetry that has rules but which doesn't work bijective). As a player or character you could of course treat your concrete version of TBA as a science.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's got more to do with what I think MyWifeIsScary was saying about how it's necessary to believe in magic. I assume that Thin-Blood Alchemy works as a way to exploit fantastic (to us) laws of nature to produce a useful expected result, which is to say that it's a technology and the results depend on what one does, not directly on what one believes. It sounds like alchemy can be magic or technology. Although I vaguely recall reading that the ancient Egyptians didn't distinguish between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 06-30-2020, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T13:12:46-07:00","id":1400165,"title":"","content":"<br /> Inceptors didn't need to be thin blooded, they needed to be clanless. Antes, arguably, weren't inceptors since they might've raided the garden of lilith, but all those little bloodlines? They've incepted disciplines and aren't composed entirely of high gens. Thinbloods just get the limelight because <i>every single one of them is clanless</i>. <br /> <br /> Thinbloods are the result of an weakened blood. That means -You have an unusually low maximum for disciplines and you're not a complete vampire but you're enough of a vampire that if you had a mage avatar it'd be destroyed- You are between a vampire and a ghoul, meaning you have less than a vampire but more than a ghoul (wait, do ghouls get disciplines in V5?) There is no sweet spot on the slider where you should get special 'alchemy'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T13:27:08-07:00","id":1400168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1400165#post1400165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinbloods are the result of an weakened blood. That means -You have an unusually low maximum for disciplines and you're not a complete vampire but you're enough of a vampire that if you had a mage avatar it'd be destroyed- You are between a vampire and a ghoul, meaning you have less than a vampire but more than a ghoul (wait, do ghouls get disciplines in V5?) There is no sweet spot on the slider where you should get special 'alchemy'</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I'm not thinking about inceptors so much as the thin-blood only merits like <i>Seer</i> aka <i>Insight</i>, which can't be taken if you're thirteenth-gen or lower. Similarly, even in the V20 era, thinbloods have more versatile blood than even Caitiff: &quot;All Kindred, but thin-bloods in particular, find their powers alter with the kind of blood consumed.&quot; (BJD 142).<br /> <br /> Alchemy is, to my reading, intended to be an extension and application of this versatility. Thinblood vitae is adaptable to a wide variety of powers, and Alchemy is a method of bringing out some of those powers in new forms.<br /> <br /> (Side note, yes, ghouls get disciplines from their regnants in V5. Revenants get even more due to the weirdness of their lineage.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T14:13:59-07:00","id":1400174,"title":"","content":"BJD was made with V5 in mind, and Dawkins to my knowledge pushed resonance and had a big sway with BJD, BJD was less 'the V20 era&quot; and more V20 signing off. <br /> <br /> I'd say insight is really the result of Methuselah supressing certain things in their lineages but only to a certain point where the blood is weak enough. <br /> <br /> So, do thinbloods get disciplines in V5? <br /> <br /> Another thing. <br /> Elder blood used to give you short term disciplines. <br /> <br /> Some alchemy powers are cool, but metaphyiscally thinbloods shouldn't be more capable of alchemy than full-blooded vampires. Thinbloods have <i>mostly</i> changed, full bloods have completely changed; they should do more. The act of embrace is alchemy and thinbloods are a halfbaked product that need completing, not their own special potions class.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T14:24:21-07:00","id":1400175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1400168#post1400168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Side note, yes, ghouls get disciplines from their regnants in V5. Revenants get even more due to the weirdness of their lineage.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least this gives me hope that if they ever get around to Dhampirs they\u2019ll at least somewhat resemble their Revised/V20 selves instead of being retconned like the Thin-blooded to have weird powers they never had before.<br /> <br /> Which of the V5 books has the Revenant content?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T14:52:17-07:00","id":1400180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1400174#post1400174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BJD was made with V5 in mind, and Dawkins to my knowledge pushed resonance and had a big sway with BJD, BJD was less 'the V20 era&quot; and more V20 signing off.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, not really. It was meant to be the set up for 4th Edition (separate from V20) but then V:TM got bought when it was almost done and they were asked to include some ties to V5.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T14:57:04-07:00","id":1400181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1400175#post1400175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which of the V5 books has the Revenant content?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chicago by Night. Right now, no great detail, just some mechanics for a Tremere having a Ducheski revenant. (Namely, they start with one free dot of Auspex and one free dot of Blood Sorcery due to being a revenant.)<br /> <br /> Hopefully when we see the Tzimisce writeup there will be more details on revenants there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T15:01:32-07:00","id":1400182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1400174#post1400174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, do thinbloods get disciplines in V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, they cannot buy disciplines and gain none at character creation. There's a merit they can take that lets them buy a single discipline at out-of-clan cost.<br /> <br /> However, they <i>can</i> get temporary disciplines based on the blood that they drink: feed from an athlete and you might get a temporary dot of Celerity or Potence, for example. This is the idea that led to Alchemy (as established in BJD).<br /> <br /> In this regard they're similar to ghouls, who now gain basic disciplines from their regnant's blood. (So for example, if I'm a Malk with Auspex 3 and Obfuscate 0, and I create a ghoul, that ghoul can get Auspex but can't get Obfuscate: what matters isn't the <i>potential</i> in my Blood, but what's been <i>realized</i> in it. If I go learn some Obfuscate and feed the ghoul again, that could change.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T15:03:06-07:00","id":1400185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1400174#post1400174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BJD was made with V5 in mind, and Dawkins to my knowledge pushed resonance and had a big sway with BJD, BJD was less 'the V20 era&quot; and more V20 signing off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the mechanics in BJD are very much V20, not V5. And it was published long before the V5 corebook was written. I don't think it's fair to call it a V5 product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T15:11:45-07:00","id":1400189,"title":"","content":"It was? Ok. For some reason I thought BJD came out after V5.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1400182#post1400182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By default, they cannot buy disciplines and gain none at character creation. There's a merit they can take that lets them buy a single discipline at out-of-clan cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why though? You had a maximum of 4/3 disciplines for thinbloods IIRC; That's potentially impressive. Is there fluff saying the blood changed or is this a retcon?<br /> <br /> It's absurd: To be less capable than a ghoul when it comes to disciplines. I guess part of this comes from the way V5 now does disciplines... Does nobody care for internal logic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T15:52:57-07:00","id":1400197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398671-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-thin-bloods-in-v5?p=1400189#post1400189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why though? You had a maximum of 4/3 disciplines for thinbloods IIRC; That's potentially impressive. Is there fluff saying the blood changed or is this a retcon?<br /> <br /> It's absurd: To be less capable than a ghoul when it comes to disciplines. I guess part of this comes from the way V5 now does disciplines... Does nobody care for internal logic?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a retcon as far as I know.<br /> <br /> And the idea is that both ghouls and thinbloods gain disciplines through the blood they consume; thinbloods are just better at it (getting it from mortal blood as well as vitae). Ghouls no longer buy disciplines with xp, they just gain them from the blood they drink, and lose them if they stop being a ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}